Write a Python module that decides the next thing the intake agent should
say to the patient, in Spanish, given the conversation so far.

Interface:

    next_turn(state: dict) -> str

state has "transcript" (turns so far) and "intake" (the partial structured
intake built so far by pipeline.build_intake).

Behavior:
- Ask exactly one clarifying question at a time, in this reference order
  when the fields are not yet populated: chief complaint, onset/timing,
  severity 0-10, associated symptoms, current medications, allergies (see
  SPEC.md for the exact reference wording).
- Never ask about a field that is already populated in intake.
- Once every required field is populated, return the confirmation recap
  ("Gracias. Permitame confirmar...") summarizing what was captured, in
  Spanish, and stop advancing the turn loop.
- If intake["triage_priority"] == "EMERGENT", say so first: acknowledge the
  red flag and state that the clinical team is being notified immediately,
  then continue with any remaining required fields.

Never invent a symptom, medication, or answer on the patient's behalf.
Raise ResponderError if state is missing "transcript" or "intake".
